sections.text:
Chausar is free. It runs on Windows and Linux laptops. There is no Mac version yet.

You need:

- a laptop with Windows 10 or 11, or a Linux laptop;
- an internet connection;
- a ChatGPT plan, a Claude plan, or an AI key (see part 2).

1. Open an invoice in **Money**, then **Invoices**.
2. Under **How clients pay**, click **Set up**.
3. Fill in what you use:
 - **UPI ID** (like yourname@okbank) and **Name clients see**;
 - bank details: **Account name**, **Account number**, **IFSC**, **Bank name**, and **SWIFT code, for clients abroad**;
 - **Days until an invoice is due** (7 days unless you change it);
 - **Payment terms on each invoice**;
 - **Reminder days late, with commas** (3, 10 and 30 unless you change them).
4. Click **Save**.

These settings work only on the computer, not from a phone.

Open the issued invoice. Under **How clients pay** you now see:

- a UPI QR code for the exact amount still owed;
- your **UPI ID** and the **Amount to pay**;
- **Copy UPI link**, a link you can send; it opens a UPI app with the amount filled in;
- your bank details.

Then use:

- **Save file** to save the invoice as a PDF;
- **Email it**. In the desktop app, your own mail app opens an email with the invoice PDF attached; check it and send it there. Some mail apps open it without a Send button: then use Forward or Edit as new. If the client has no email in Chausar (or one a mail link cannot carry), add the address in your mail app. If this computer has no mail app for email files, Chausar opens a mail link with the words filled in instead, and **Show the PDF in its folder** shows the file to attach. In the browser it opens a mail link, and you attach the file yourself.
- **Share on WhatsApp**. The WhatsApp desktop app opens if this computer has it, otherwise WhatsApp in your browser, with the message ready. A WhatsApp link cannot carry a file, so attach the PDF yourself: **Show the PDF in its folder** shows where it is.
- Chausar sends nothing: you press send yourself each time.
